title: '[eth-rpc] Store receipts at index time'

doc:
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    `eth-rpc` stores the receipt and the signed transaction of every transaction it indexes, in
    the same database transaction as the transaction hashes and logs. `eth_getTransactionReceipt`,
    `eth_getBlockReceipts`, `eth_getTransactionByHash`, `eth_getTransactionByBlockHashAndIndex`
    and `eth_getTransactionByBlockNumberAndIndex` read receipts and transactions from the
    database. They no longer fetch the block body and events from the node or make the
    `eth_receipt_data` and `eth_block_hash` runtime calls. Stored receipts are removed with the
    rest of a block's data when the block is pruned from the `eth-rpc` database or replaced by a
    fork.

    `eth_getTransactionReceipt`, `eth_getTransactionByHash` and
    `eth_getTransactionByBlockHashAndIndex` do not contact the node at all for a block with
    stored receipts, so they keep answering for blocks the node has pruned.
    `eth_getBlockReceipts` and `eth_getTransactionByBlockNumberAndIndex` still resolve the block
    through the node first, so they depend on the node still having the block.

    Against a local dev node, the median latency went from 1.08 ms to 0.13 ms for
    `eth_getTransactionReceipt`, from 2.1 ms to 0.12 ms for `eth_getTransactionByHash` and from
    1.6 ms to 0.46 ms for `eth_getBlockReceipts` (blocks of 5 to 80 transactions). The database
    grows by about 1.1 KB of payload per indexed transaction (a JSON receipt without logs and the
    RLP encoded transaction), about 1.4 KiB on disk including the table's primary key index.

    On start, `eth-rpc` applies database migration `0005_create_receipts`. It creates the
    `receipts` table and adds a `receipts_version` column to `eth_to_substrate_blocks`. Nothing
    needs to be done by hand. Blocks indexed before the upgrade are not backfilled: their receipts
    are rebuilt from the node on request, as for any block without stored receipts. To store
    receipts for all blocks, index into a new database.

    Stored receipts keep what receipt extraction produced when the block was indexed. A later
    `eth-rpc` release that fixes receipt extraction reaches already indexed blocks only if it also
    bumps the stored format version (`RECEIPTS_VERSION`), which makes those blocks fall back to
    the node, or if the blocks are indexed again into a new database.

    Downgrading to an `eth-rpc` without this migration against the same database fails on start
    with the sqlx migration error `VersionMissing(5)`. Keep a copy of the database from before
    the upgrade, or index into a new database, if a downgrade may be needed.

    `eth-rpc` keeps working with the same runtime versions as before: receipts are built through
    the same runtime calls, once per block when it is indexed.
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Code using `pallet-revive-eth-rpc` as a library needs these changes:

    - `ReceiptProvider::block_receipts` returns `Vec<ReceiptInfo>` instead of
      `Vec<(TransactionSigned, ReceiptInfo)>`. It serves the receipts stored at index time and
      rebuilds them from the node only when they are not stored. To get the signed transactions
      of a block, call `ReceiptExtractor::extract_from_block`.
    - `ReceiptProvider::signed_tx_by_hash` and `Client::signed_tx_by_hash` are removed. Use
      `ReceiptProvider::transaction_by_hash` or `Client::transaction`, which return the signed
      transaction together with its receipt.
    - New: `ReceiptProvider::transaction_by_block_hash_and_index` and
      `Client::transaction_by_hash_and_index` return the signed transaction and receipt at a
      Substrate block hash and transaction index.

    Before:

    ```rust
    let receipts: Vec<ReceiptInfo> = provider
        .block_receipts(&block)
        .await?
        .into_iter()
        .map(|(_, receipt)| receipt)
        .collect();
    let signed_tx = client.signed_tx_by_hash(&hash).await;
    ```

    After:

    ```rust
    let receipts: Vec<ReceiptInfo> = provider.block_receipts(&block).await?;
    let signed_tx = client.transaction(&hash).await.map(|(signed_tx, _)| signed_tx);
    ```

crates:
- name: pallet-revive-eth-rpc
  bump: major
